# 2. Ubuntu vs Alpine

## Why Is Alpine Much Smaller?

Alpine Linux is designed to be a small and minimal Linux distribution.

It contains only the essential components required to run applications.

Ubuntu is a more feature-rich general-purpose Linux distribution and includes considerably more packages and utilities.

```text
Alpine
   ↓
Minimal Linux distribution
   ↓
Smaller image

Ubuntu
   ↓
More packages and utilities
   ↓
Larger image
```

### My Understanding

The smaller size of Alpine can be useful when building lightweight Docker images, especially when the application does not require the additional packages provided by a larger distribution.

