# 32. Real-World Troubleshooting Connection

The practical commands I learned today can be directly connected to production troubleshooting.

For example, if a containerized application is not working, I can start with:

```bash
docker ps
```

Then check:

```bash
docker logs <container>
```

Inspect the container:

```bash
docker inspect <container>
```

Check networking information:

```bash
docker inspect <container>
```

Execute commands inside the container:

```bash
docker exec -it <container> bash
```

Check filesystem usage:

```bash
docker exec <container> df -h
```

This gives me a structured approach:

```text
Application Issue
       ↓
Is container running?
       ↓
docker ps
       ↓
Check logs
       ↓
docker logs
       ↓
Inspect configuration
       ↓
docker inspect
       ↓
Check network / ports
       ↓
docker inspect
       ↓
Enter container if required
       ↓
docker exec
```

